IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `miles-card-domain`
IMPORT `miles-card`
IMPORT `cheatsheet-claims`

§ `Cheat-sheet claims the primary text does not support`

-- ===========================================================================
-- WHAT THIS FILE IS. The household cheat sheet ([S5], June 2026, a secondary
-- source, not committed) makes claims about what each card earns. Those
-- claims are deposited as the additional encoding `cheatsheet-2026-06`
-- (cheatsheet-claims.l4) and run through the pipeline's p6-tests stage as
-- the corpus's acceptance test (spec section 1). Every claim that stage
-- proved unsupported by the issuer's own text is restated HERE as an
-- `#ASSERT NOT (...)`, with the cheat-sheet cell and the clause that
-- contradicts it, so that the committed corpus is green while the
-- discrepancy stays on the record and a rule change that quietly made the
-- cheat sheet right again would trip it.
--
-- FILLED FROM THE FORMAL ACCEPTANCE RUN, NOT FROM A HAND READING. Run
-- `2026-09-21-2e987f68-001`, p6-tests DEGRADED, receipt
-- `sha256:8894658530171acc57ac6e2f2e461f865db8afd1fccbd0af39b2340139639557`:
-- 184 assertions over `cheatsheet-2026-06`, 129 satisfied, 55 failed. All 55
-- are triaged below. The pre-pass snapshot, and the two pre-registered
-- discrepancies this run had to surface without being told where to look,
-- are in etc/go/subjects/sg-miles-card/NOTES.md section 5.
--
-- HOW EACH ROW IS WRITTEN. Every failure carries the [S5] cell verbatim, the
-- line of cheatsheet-claims.l4 it failed at, a classification letter, and
-- the clause of the held document that settles it, quoted. Then the cheat
-- sheet's own claim, negated; and, where the encoding answers a specific
-- other value, that value asserted positively, so this file records what the
-- text DOES say and not only what it does not.
--
-- THE FOUR CLASSIFICATIONS, and what each one licenses.
--   (a) THE CHEAT SHEET IS WRONG ON THE TEXT. A clause of a held document
--       contradicts the cell. The household is routing spend on a figure the
--       issuer does not owe. 9 failures.
--   (b) THE ENCODING IS WRONG. The cheat sheet is right and a card module
--       misreads its own document. NONE FOUND, and this file would be the
--       wrong place for one: a category (b) finding is a bug against the
--       module, not a disputed cheat-sheet claim, and writing it here would
--       freeze the defect as the expected answer. The triage report,
--       `ACCEPTANCE-TRIAGE.md` beside this file, records what was checked.
--   (c) GENUINELY CONDITIONAL. The answer turns on the merchant's system
--       indicator, which three issuers say in terms they do not determine
--       (DBS Woman's cl.13, Citi cl.6(ii), HSBC cl.6). The cardholder cannot
--       observe it at the moment of paying, so every fixture carries
--       `Unknown` and the headline `miles per dollar` is the LOWER branch.
--       The cheat sheet's cell is the UPPER branch, stated as though the
--       indicator were settled. Neither party is wrong about a rate; they
--       are answering different questions. 18 failures.
--   (d) THE FIGURE RESTS ON A DOCUMENT THIS CORPUS DOES NOT HOLD, OR ON ONE
--       THAT HAS EXPIRED, OR ON ROUNDING. 28 failures.
--
-- WHY NO CELL IS "CORRECTED". A claim edited to match the answer destroys
-- the only evidence the comparison produces. The expressions below are
-- copied from cheatsheet-claims.l4 unchanged, negated in place, and the
-- fixtures are that file's own -- imported, never redefined, so a change to
-- a fixture moves both files together or neither.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `UOB Lady's Solitaire -- the sheet's 6 is the T&C's 4, plus an uplift no held document states`

-- The cheat sheet prints "Solitaire (6, S$750)" on ten rows and explains the
-- figure once, as "4 card + 2 savings". The card half is exactly what the
-- held T&C states; the savings half is an uplift for holding a UOB Lady's
-- Savings Account, and no document in source/ says it exists, let alone what
-- it pays. So the sheet is not wrong about the CARD -- it is quoting a total
-- this corpus cannot check, and the module answers the card's own figure and
-- says so in a condition ("A Lady's Savings Account uplift above 4 miles per
-- S$1 is NOT in this document and is unconfirmed here").
--
-- The document states the 4 twice, by two routes, which is why this is a
-- clean (d) and not an argument:
--   [uob-ladys-cards-tnc heading A] "A. Preferred Rewards Category(ies)
--     Spending - 10X UNI$ per S$5 spent (equivalent to 4 miles per S$1 spent)"
--   [uob-ladys-cards-tnc cl.2(b)] "Base UNI$" means the reward of UNI$1 for
--     every S$5.00 spent (equivalent to 0.4 miles per S$1 spent)
--   [uob-ladys-cards-tnc cl.2(c)] "Bonus UNI$" means the bonus reward of 9X
--     UNI$ per S$5 spent (equivalent to 3.6 miles per S$1 ...) -- 0.4 + 3.6 = 4
--
-- The cap the same cells print, S$750, is NOT disputed: cl.6(b) states it and
-- every cap assertion on these rows passed. Only the rate is here.

-- [S5] "Dining out (restaurants, MCC 5811/5812) | Lady's Solitaire -- Dining (6, S$750)"
-- (d) cheatsheet-claims.l4:349 claims 6; the text answers 4.
-- [uob-ladys-cards-tnc heading A] "10X UNI$ per S$5 spent (equivalent to 4 miles per S$1 spent)"
#ASSERT NOT ((`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 dining out`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 6)
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 dining out`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 4

-- [S5] "Cafes / coffee shops / bubble tea (indie; MCC 5812/5814) | Solitaire -- Dining (6, S$750)"
-- (d) cheatsheet-claims.l4:364 claims 6; the text answers 4.
-- [uob-ladys-cards-tnc heading A] "10X UNI$ per S$5 spent (equivalent to 4 miles per S$1 spent)"
#ASSERT NOT ((`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 a cafe`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 6)
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 a cafe`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 4

-- [S5] "Solitaire -- Family (6, S$750)"
