§§ `DBS yuu -- 10 is 10.08 and ~S$822 is S$822.86: the sheet rounds`

-- Both figures are the sheet compressing, and both compress in the direction
-- that understates. A yuu Merchant purchase in a month above the threshold
-- earns cl.6's 1 Base Point plus cl.7(a)'s 9 and cl.7(b)'s 26 = 36 yuu Points
-- per S$1, and cl.12 values a point at 0.28 miles: 36 x 0.28 = 10.08.
--   [dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.12] "1 yuu Point is equivalent to 0.5% cash rebate
--     or 0.28 miles or more, depending on the redemption item on the yuu
--     Rewards catalogue."
-- The cap is stated in POINTS, so it needs no conversion, and the sheet's own
-- "~S$822" is that cap divided by the 35 BONUS points per S$1:
--   [dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.7] "Total Bonus Rewards is capped at 28,800 yuu
--     Points (worth up to S$144 cash rebates or 8,000 miles) per calendar
--     month."   28,800 / 35 = S$822.857...
--
-- THE ADDITIVE READING IS A LIVE FORK, not a settled figure: fork-register
-- entry `F-yuu-bonus-additive` records that no clause says the two Bonus
-- Rewards tables add, which is why the module marks these answers
-- `Unconfirmed`. It does not change the classification -- on the rejected
-- `replacement` reading the rate would be 7.56, further from the sheet's 10,
-- not nearer.

-- [S5] "Cold Storage / CS Fresh / Giant (yuu, MCC 5411) | DBS yuu (10, S$822)"
-- (d) cheatsheet-claims.l4:380 claims 10; the text answers 10.08.
-- [dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.12] "1 yuu Point is equivalent to ... 0.28 miles or more" -- 36 points x 0.28 = 10.08
#ASSERT NOT ((`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 cold storage`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 10)
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 cold storage`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 10.08

-- [S5] "Cold Storage / CS Fresh / Giant (yuu, MCC 5411) | DBS yuu (10, S$822)"
-- (d) cheatsheet-claims.l4:381 claims 822; the text answers 28800 / 35.
-- [dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.7] "Total Bonus Rewards is capped at 28,800 yuu Points ... per calendar month" -- 28,800 / 35
#ASSERT NOT ((`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 cold storage`)'s `cap`'s `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 822)
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 cold storage`)'s `cap`'s `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 28800 / 35

-- [S5] "foodpanda / food delivery (MCC 5814) | DBS yuu (10, S$822)"
-- (d) cheatsheet-claims.l4:439 claims 10; the text answers 10.08.
-- [dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.12] "1 yuu Point is equivalent to ... 0.28 miles or more" -- 36 points x 0.28 = 10.08
#ASSERT NOT ((`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 a foodpanda order`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 10)
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 a foodpanda order`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 10.08

-- [S5] "foodpanda / food delivery (MCC 5814) | DBS yuu (10, S$822)"
-- (d) cheatsheet-claims.l4:440 claims 822; the text answers 28800 / 35.
-- [dbs-yuu-card-tnc cl.7] "Total Bonus Rewards is capped at 28,800 yuu Points ... per calendar month" -- 28,800 / 35
#ASSERT NOT ((`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 a foodpanda order`)'s `cap`'s `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 822)
